{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/624479-converting-hunter-the-reckoning-edges-to-hunter-the-vigil","id":624479,"title":"Converting Hunter the Reckoning Edges to Hunter The Vigil","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-12T10:42:58-07:00","id":624479,"title":"Converting Hunter the Reckoning Edges to Hunter The Vigil","content":"Hello everyone, I'm new to posting on the Onyx forums and I need help.<br /> <br /> I've melded cosmologies and mechanics from the old system to the new with the help of the Translation guides, unfortunately there is no translation guide for Hunter.<br /> <br /> I need help converting the 2-Dot Edge power for Defenders which is Rejuvenate:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> System: Your character\u2019s health levels lost through bashing<br /> damage heal at a rate of one every 10 minutes. Lethal damage heals according to the following chart. These rates supersede normal recovery times, but are still cumulative. (It takes 21 hours to recover fully from Injured, for example.)<br /> <br /> Health Level Recovery Time<br /> Bruised Three hours<br /> Hurt Six hours<br /> Injured 12 hours<br /> Wounded One day<br /> Mauled Three days<br /> Crippled One week<br /> Incapacitated Three weeks<br /> <br /> The Defender lays his hands upon a subject to heal the injuries of another. Spend Conviction to restore a subject\u2019s most severe wound (her \u201clowest\u201d lost level). One Conviction must be spent to restore a level lost to bashing damage. Two Conviction must be spent to restore a level lost to lethal damage. That health level is restored in the same time it takes a Defender with this edge to recuperate, as indicated above \u2014 10 minutes for a level lost to bashing damage, one day for a Wounded level lost to lethal damage, for example. Healing can be applied to other imbued, humans and even willing supernatural creatures that possess bodies. Destroyed is destroyed, of course, no matter who the recipient of this power is. Conviction cannot be used to enhance this edge; its effects occur automatically. Rejuvenate applies to healing health levels only; the edge does not increase recovery time from drug or alcohol abuse, or counteract poisons that do not reduce health levels, for example. Likewise, the edge does not cure any long-term illness such as cancer or re-grow lost appendages. </div> </div> </div>Any guidance on translating the mechanics to the new system would be greatly appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7264,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7264-sawrunner8","user":"SAWrunner8","date":". 08-12-2015, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7264-sawrunner8","name":"SAWrunner8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7264_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T11:58:33-07:00","id":624530,"title":"","content":"The easiest way to convert a bunch of Edges, I find, is to rename and refluff Benedictions and Castigations; you can actually see where a few of them were inspired by Reckoning Edges (Wrathful Sword of St. Michael the Archangel, pp. 163-164, being a new take on Cleave, for example). There's lay-on-hands healing in the corebook in the form of The Hands of St. Luke, p. 160.<br /> <br /> The major difference is that the Benediction doesn't confer passive rejuvenation to the hunter who possesses it. You could split Rejuvenate into two Endowments, one being The Hands of St. Luke and one that splits the hunter's healing times in half (so ~8h/1B, one day/1L, one week/1A). Or you could simply convert Rejuvenate over more directly, which I'd probably do with the halved healing times and an activation cost of one Willpower/Conviction per 2B or 1L (depending on if you're using Conviction pools or just Willpower for your Imbued). I don't well recall how plentiful or constrained Conviction supplies are, so if you're using Conviction and that's too effective, you could ratchet down to one Conviction per 1B, or one Conviction to reduce 1L to 1B.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T13:05:17-07:00","id":624558,"title":"","content":"That helps a lot, I'm actually bringing over the Creeds from Reckoning to Vigil and have Imbuing as a 4-Dot Merit if they want access to the Edges as &quot;Creed Endowments&quot;. Along with any other endowments associated with their compact or conspiracy. I'll be using their Willpower for the activation of these abilities.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7264-sawrunner8","name":"SAWrunner8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7264_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T13:59:29-07:00","id":624622,"title":"","content":"That's pretty much exactly how I'd do it, except for the four-dot buy-in. Four dots is steep just to qualify to buy something else; just in general, buying a dot should do something for you in the moment. I'd either reduce the cost or afford additional benefits from the base Merit buy-in. Something like...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Reckoning (\u25cf-\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</b></span><br /> The Imbued appear scattershot across the world. Many never find one another at all, and many more have little contact with their fellow hunters. If they are a conspiracy, the true conspirators are the unknown energies by whom they are invested and contacted. As such, this Merit replaces the Status Merit used by other conspiracies, and measures the depth of the character's connection to these energies. Hunters with comrades among the Imbued, such as active personalities on hunter-net, should purchase the Allies (Imbued) Merit to represent backup.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Once you accept the Call, you cannot turn back. When you go for a week or more ignoring opportunities to answer the call, or witness an immediate crisis and avoid involving yourself in some way, nightmares of recrimination plague you, and your fitful sleep recovers no Willpower. The nightmares continue until you once again answer the call.<br /> <br /> <b>Calling (\u25cf): </b>You still face breaking points from supernatural shocks, but don't suffer exaggerated responses to supernatural exposure, such as the Lunacy imposed by werewolves or the Quiescence provoked by supernal sorcery. You receive the Unseen Sense Merit for free, relating to whatever creatures the Messengers choose as your quarry.<br /> <b>Creed (\u25cf\u25cf): </b>Gain access to your Creed Endowments. You receive a single one-dot Endowment for free.<br /> <b>Conviction (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf): </b>Add your dots in Reckoning when you roll against a breaking point in pursuit of your Creed.<br /> <b>Confrontation (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf): </b>Your second sight deepens. You may call upon your Unseen Sense any number of times per chapter. Add half your dots in Reckoning, rounded up, as a Supernatural Tolerance trait against a creature you have found with your second sight.<br /> <b>Contact (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf): </b>Your awareness brushes against the source of the Imbuing itself. Once per chapter, you can concentrate on a question to ask the source directly. Its answer may be as vague or indirect as the Storyteller chooses, but it is never untrue or misleading. If it is of no practical help, the chapter's use is not expended.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T10:25:48-07:00","id":625674,"title":"","content":"Nice.... I'll bring this layout to my players and get their take on it. Thanks again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7264-sawrunner8","name":"SAWrunner8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7264_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}